  "userRequest": "Can we figure out a way for the mcpb to work launching a local web experience that's similar to the desktop app? I'm also still hitting issues with both mcpb and desktop app actually launching and working; investigate and debug.",
  "description": "Added an open_dashboard MCP tool that launches a local, offline web dashboard from the .mcpb — a browser view of the Wellframe health data served on 127.0.0.1, backed by six /api routes reading the real local SQLite through the existing sql.js layer. Each desktop data loader gained a native then web-API then fixture tier so the same desktop frontend renders real data when served by the mcpb; pack.sh bundles the desktop build into the .mcpb, and 11 unit tests cover the row-mapping and index.html-rewrite logic. Also root-caused the launch issues: the mcpb boots cleanly and the desktop app code is sound — frontend renders headless with zero errors and the Rust shell compiles — isolating the failure to the native Tauri packaging layer.",
